{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZUnitModulusPrune","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KZUnitModulusPrune","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Trigonometric","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZUnitModulusPrune.exp_I_ne_real_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZUnitModulusPrune.exp_I_ne_real_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZUnitModulusPrune.lean#L35-L43","doc":"The same statement as an inequality on the complex number itself: `exp(iθ) ≠ q` for real\n`q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZUnitModulusPrune.unit_modulus_ne_real_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZUnitModulusPrune.unit_modulus_ne_real_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZUnitModulusPrune.lean#L28-L33","doc":"**C-prune.** A monodromy eigenvalue of the form `exp(iθ)` with `θ` real has modulus one, so it\nis never a real number greater than one — in particular never the substrate pin `q₀ ≈ 1.11`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}